C. Incorrect. Consistent standards are important, but identical behavior with every client is neither necessary nor always clinically appropriate. Boundary decisions may require consideration of the client’s culture, age, vulnerability, treatment needs, and clinical setting.
D. Incorrect. Clinicians may naturally experience protectiveness, frustration, identification, attraction, or other emotional reactions. The ethical concern is how those reactions are managed and whether they begin to interfere with professional judgment.
