C. Incorrect. A therapist should not wait for a complaint before responding to a foreseeable concern. Clients may not recognize unhealthy dependency or may fear that raising the issue will jeopardize treatment.
D. Correct. The therapist should evaluate how the pattern of late-night availability is affecting role clarity, autonomy, and treatment. The client’s increasing reliance on the therapist for ordinary decisions suggests that the communication pattern may be encouraging dependency. A client-centered response would include discussing what has developed, clarifying when and how messages will be handled, identifying appropriate crisis procedures, and monitoring whether the client becomes more able to function independently.
