C. Incorrect. Discussing foreseeable overlap is an appropriate safeguard. It promotes transparency and allows the therapist and client to plan for possible concerns.
D. Incorrect. Consultation is a responsible method of identifying risks and protecting client welfare. It does not itself create a conflict of interest.
CTA Exam Strategy: A multiple relationship describes the roles. A conflict of interest describes the competing interest that may interfere with professional responsibility.',
