B. Correct. Repeated and escalating gifts create more concern than a single modest gesture. The pattern may reflect increasing attachment, dependency, an attempt to influence treatment, fear of rejection, or an expectation of reciprocity. The therapist should discuss the pattern respectfully, assess its effect on treatment, clarify boundaries, and determine whether continued acceptance would create obligation or impair objectivity.
