CTA Exam Strategy: When the question involves sexual conduct with a current client, do not choose an answer that merely recommends: Risk-benefit analysis; Client consent; Documentation; A waiver; Moving the conduct outside therapy; The therapist must maintain the boundary and not engage in the relationship.',
